# Cloudflare Pages. Only the app's own paths answer with the app. A top-level 404.html (made by
# the build, see vite.config.ts) turns Pages' automatic single-page fallback off, so everything
# else, /v1/* included, is a real 404 instead of the app with a 200. The rewrite goes to /, not
# /index.html, which Pages redirects to /. Tested on a preview deployment (docs/adr/0008).
/matches / 200
/matches/ / 200
/match/* / 200
/players/* / 200
/compare / 200
/compare/ / 200
